<%!-- Hidden JS-hook anchors. When embedded inside a parent surface
     (e.g. MeetingLive), the parent already mounts these hooks; mounting
     them a second time would create duplicate elements with the same id
     (LiveKit Room would double-subscribe). Suppress them in embedded
     mode and let the parent own the singletons. --%>
<div :if={!@embedded} id="push-subscribe" phx-hook="PushSubscribe" class="hidden"></div>

<div :if={!@embedded} id="chat-state" phx-hook="ChatState" class="hidden"></div>

<%!-- data-camera-enabled / data-mic-enabled carry the server's committed
     media intent. On a LiveKit reconnect (task 019e4b3e stage 3) the JS
     hook reads these off the dataset to re-engage the camera/mic WITHOUT
     waiting for a fresh LV push — reconnect-safe (Rowan's exact error was
     "unable to push hook event. LiveView not connected"). --%>
<div
  :if={!@embedded}
  id="meeting-client"
  phx-hook="MeetingClient"
  class="hidden"
  data-camera-enabled={to_string(@camera_enabled)}
  data-mic-enabled={to_string(@mic_enabled)}
>
</div>
<div :if={!@embedded} id="meeting-room" phx-hook="MeetingRoom" class="hidden"></div>
<div :if={!@embedded} id="meeting-soundboard" phx-hook="MeetingSoundboard" class="hidden"></div>

<.notification_banner :if={!@embedded} push_permission={@push_permission} />

<%!-- Chat root must claim the full height of <main> AND set min-h-0 so its
     descendant flex columns (chat-drop-zone, #message-list) can correctly
     shrink-to-fit. Without min-h-0, the default `min-height: auto` on flex
     items lets long message lists push past the viewport — on iOS Safari /
     PWA standalone, this manifests as the bottom-tab nav being pushed
     below the visible area while messages scroll the document itself.
     PR #333 rooted the shell chrome but the chat surface was still
     blowing the layout from the inside. --%>
<div class="flex h-full min-h-0 overflow-hidden">
  <%!-- Desktop sidebar — sectioned channel rail (chat plan v2 Stage 2).

       The `hidden lg:flex` responsive gate keeps this whole rail invisible
       on mobile; the mobile flat-list path lives in the `mobile_browser_open`
       overlay below and is intentionally untouched. Same pattern as the
       icon-rail / bottom-rail split in shell.html.heex.

       Section order:
         1. Pinned   (renders only when non-empty; locked at top)
         2. DMs      (always shown; renders empty-state when no DMs)
         3. Sub-orgs (Paragon / Soylent / Fabrikam / Wayne-Tech / SXI, ALWAYS
                      rendered as section headers — empty buckets get an
                      empty-state hint instead of being suppressed)

       Stage 3 will wire drag-and-drop on the `.channel-section-drag-handle`
       affordance; today it's a static `☰` glyph that fades in on hover. --%>
  <aside
    :if={!@embedded}
    id="chat-sidebar"
    phx-hook="ResizableSidebar"
    class="hidden lg:flex relative flex-shrink-0 flex-col border-r border-base-content/10 bg-base-200"
  >
    <%!-- Sidebar header (chat sidebar Stage 5). Hosts the "Edit layout" /
         "Done" toggle. In edit mode the rail shows per-channel grab handles,
         per-section Hide/Show controls, keyboard move buttons, and a "Reset
         to default layout" action; in normal mode the rail navigates as
         before. Desktop only — the whole aside is `hidden lg:flex`. --%>
    <%!-- Sidebar header. The ~260px rail can't fit two text toggles, so the
         personal "Edit layout" and admin "Edit default" entry points collapse
         into ONE overflow ("More") menu (ui-ux-pro overflow-menu pattern: when
         actions exceed available space, use an overflow menu instead of
         cramming).

         Overflow contract — this row must NEVER push content past the ~260px
         rail in ANY mode. Containment comes from the flex children, NOT from
         clipping the row: the row is `min-w-0`, the text child truncates
         (`flex-1 min-w-0 truncate`), and the action button is pinned
         (`flex-shrink-0`). We deliberately do NOT put `overflow-hidden` on
         this row — the normal-mode "More" popover is anchored inside it and
         opens BELOW it (`top-full`), so an `overflow-hidden` row would clip
         the menu off (it did: the dropdown rendered hidden behind the rail).
           * in EITHER edit mode we do NOT also render the word "CHANNELS" —
             the mode label IS the row's text and takes the remaining space
             (`flex-1 min-w-0 truncate`), with only the "Done" button pinned
             (`flex-shrink-0`). The mode label + accent already say which mode
             is active, so "Done" needs no "(admin)" qualifier;
           * in normal mode the "CHANNELS" label is the flex-1 truncating child
             and the kebab "More" button is pinned (`flex-shrink-0`). --%>
    <div class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 border-b border-base-content/10 min-w-0">
      <%= cond do %>
        <% @sidebar_edit -> %>
          <%!-- In personal-edit mode: a single "Done" exit + a quiet mode
               label that absorbs the row's free space and truncates. No other
               control — and no "CHANNELS" word — occupies the row. --%>
          <span class="channel-edit-mode-label flex-1">Editing my layout</span>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_sidebar_edit"
            class="channel-edit-toggle flex-shrink-0"
            aria-pressed="true"
            aria-label="Done editing layout"
          >
            Done
          </button>
        <% @sidebar_admin_edit -> %>
          <%!-- In admin-edit mode: a single "Done" exit + an admin-accented
               mode label so the admin always knows they are editing what
               everyone sees. The label absorbs free space and truncates; only
               "Done" is pinned. No "CHANNELS" word in the row. --%>
          <span class="channel-edit-mode-label channel-edit-mode-label--admin flex-1">
            Editing company default
          </span>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="toggle_sidebar_admin_edit"
            class="channel-admin-edit-toggle flex-shrink-0"
            aria-pressed="true"
            aria-label="Done editing the company default"
          >
            Done
          </button>
        <% true -> %>
          <%!-- Normal mode: the "CHANNELS" label (flex-1, truncates) + ONE
               compact "More" (kebab) button (flex-shrink-0). Clicking the
               button opens an absolutely-positioned popover CONTAINED within
               the aside (the wrapper is position:relative so the menu anchors
               to the header, never floats over the chat pane). The menu closes
               on click-away and Escape; choosing an item enters the mode AND
               closes the menu (handled server-side). --%>
          <p class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/60">
            Channels
          </p>
          <div class="channel-sidebar-menu relative flex-shrink-0">
            <button
              type="button"
              phx-click="toggle_sidebar_menu"
              class="channel-sidebar-menu-button"
              aria-haspopup="menu"
              aria-expanded={to_string(@sidebar_menu_open)}
              aria-label="Sidebar layout options"
            >
              <span class="hero-ellipsis-vertical size-4"></span>
            </button>
            <div
              :if={@sidebar_menu_open}
              class="channel-sidebar-menu-popover"
              role="menu"
              aria-label="Sidebar layout options"
              phx-click-away="close_sidebar_menu"
              phx-window-keydown="close_sidebar_menu"
              phx-key="escape"
            >
              <button
                type="button"
                role="menuitem"
                phx-click="toggle_sidebar_edit"
                class="channel-sidebar-menu-item"
              >
                Edit my layout
              </button>
              <%!-- Admin-only entry point. Rendered ONLY for Fabrikam admins; the
                   handler re-checks @fabrikam_admin? as the real gate. Admin accent
                   so it reads as a company-wide action, not a personal one. --%>
              <button
                :if={@fabrikam_admin?}
                type="button"
                role="menuitem"
                phx-click="toggle_sidebar_admin_edit"
                class="channel-sidebar-menu-item channel-sidebar-menu-item--admin"
              >
                Edit company default
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <nav
      id="chat-section-list"
      phx-hook="SectionReorder"
      data-sidebar-edit={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
      class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2"
      aria-label="Channel sections"
    >
      <%!-- Pinned section — only renders when non-empty.
           NOT hideable (per chat sidebar v3 Stage 2 — hide button is
           rendered on sub-org rows only). NOT reorderable — Pinned + DMs
           lock to the top of the rail. --%>
      <%= if @channel_sections.pinned != [] do %>
        <section
          class="channel-section group"
          data-section-key="pinned"
          data-section-reorderable="false"
          aria-label="Pinned"
        >
          <div class="channel-section-header">
            <span class="hero-bookmark-solid size-3.5 text-base-content/60"></span>
            <p class="channel-section-label">Pinned</p>
          </div>
          <.link
            :for={space <- @channel_sections.pinned}
            navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug || space.id}"}
            class={[
              "channel-row",
              @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
            <span class="truncate flex-1">{space.name}</span>
            <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
              <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
              </span>
            <% end %>
          </.link>
        </section>
      <% end %>

      <%!-- DMs section — always rendered, even when empty (Marlowe: empty
           sections keep their header so the rail's structure is visible).
           Section key: "dms". NOT reorderable (Stage 3) — locked under Pinned. --%>
      <section
        class="channel-section group"
        data-section-key="dms"
        data-section-reorderable="false"
        aria-label="Direct Messages"
      >
        <div class="channel-section-header">
          <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-3.5 text-base-content/60"></span>
          <p class="channel-section-label">Direct Messages</p>
          <button
            type="button"
            phx-click="new_conversation_open"
            class="text-base-content/40 hover:text-primary ml-auto"
            title="New conversation"
          >
            <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <%= if @channel_sections.dms == [] do %>
          <p class="channel-section-empty">
            No conversations yet — direct messages will appear here once you start one.
          </p>
        <% else %>
          <.link
            :for={space <- @channel_sections.dms}
            navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug || space.id}"}
            class={[
              "channel-row",
              @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="truncate flex-1">{sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}</span>
            <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
              <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
              </span>
            <% end %>
          </.link>
        <% end %>
      </section>

      <%!-- Sub-org sections (chat sidebar v3 Stage 4). Rendered from
           `@sidebar_sections` — the org-default sections (one per org,
           `channel_sections` table) merged with the user's personal
           arrangement by `Sidebar.resolve_for_user/2`. Each entry is a
           `%{section, channels}`: `section.name` is the header label,
           `section.color` is the scope token driving the org pill, and
           `channels` are the spaces placed under it by `chat_spaces.org_id`.
           ALWAYS rendered, even when empty — empty sections keep their
           header + an empty-state hint so the rail's structure stays visible.

           Filtered by @scope_filter when set (Stage 4): nil → all sections;
           an atom filter → only the section whose color matches that scope.
           The filter is toggled by clicking the chat-header scope-pill. --%>
      <% visible_sections =
        if is_nil(@scope_filter) do
          @sidebar_sections
        else
          Enum.filter(@sidebar_sections, fn %{section: section} ->
            PlatformWeb.ChatLive.section_scope_atom(section.color) == @scope_filter
          end)
        end %>
      <%!-- ChannelMembershipDrag wrapper (chat sidebar Stage 5). A SEPARATE
           hook element from the <nav>'s SectionReorder hook: an element can
           only carry one phx-hook, and the two drag behaviors target
           different draggables (channel rows here vs. section headers there).
           Both hooks are bubble-phase listeners; each ignores the other's
           dragstart source, so they coexist on overlapping DOM. The hook is
           inert unless `data-sidebar-edit="true"`. --%>
      <div
        id="channel-membership-drag"
        phx-hook="ChannelMembershipDrag"
        data-sidebar-edit={to_string(@sidebar_edit)}
        data-admin-edit={to_string(@sidebar_admin_edit)}
      >
        <section
          :for={%{section: section, channels: section_channels} <- visible_sections}
          id={"section-#{section.id}"}
          class="channel-section group"
          data-section-key={section.name}
          data-section-slug={section.color}
          data-section-id={section.id}
          data-section-reorderable="true"
          draggable="true"
          aria-label={"#{section.name} channels"}
        >
          <div class="channel-section-header">
            <%!-- Admin-edit (Stage 6): inline rename form per section header.
                 Submitting (Enter / blur via phx-change is intentionally NOT
                 used — we only persist on explicit submit so a mid-typing
                 re-render can't fire a half-typed name). The hidden section_id
                 rides along so the server knows which org-default row to
                 rename. In personal-edit and normal modes the label is static
                 text. --%>
            <%= if @sidebar_admin_edit do %>
              <form
                phx-submit="rename_section_default"
                class="channel-section-rename-form"
              >
                <input type="hidden" name="section_id" value={section.id} />
                <input
                  type="text"
                  name="name"
                  value={section.name}
                  class="channel-section-rename-input"
                  aria-label={"Rename #{section.name} section"}
                  maxlength="60"
                />
              </form>
            <% else %>
              <p class="channel-section-label">{section.name}</p>
            <% end %>
            <%!-- Color-only swatch. The section's IDENTITY text is `section.name`
                 (rendered above / in the rename input); this dot communicates
                 the section's COLOR and nothing else. Previously this slot held
                 a `<.scope_pill>` whose VISIBLE TEXT was derived from the color
                 token via the scope enum, so recoloring a section (e.g. Fabrikam →
                 yellow) silently relabeled the chip to "Paragon". Decoupling:
                 a recolor now changes ONLY this dot, never any name/label. The
                 dot is decorative (aria-hidden) — `section.name` beside it is
                 the text identity. --%>
            <%= if dot = PlatformWeb.ChatLive.section_dot_class(section.color) do %>
              <span
                class={["channel-section-color-dot", dot]}
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
              </span>
            <% end %>
            <%!-- Per-section Hide/Show control (Stage 5, edit mode only).
                 Posts the DESIRED next hidden state so the toggle is
                 idempotent. A hidden section drops out of @sidebar_sections
                 entirely (resolver behavior), so the only way to bring it
                 back is the "Reset to default layout" button below — which
                 is why we never render a Show control inline here. --%>
            <button
              :if={@sidebar_edit}
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-hide-button"
              phx-click="toggle_section_hidden"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-hidden="true"
              aria-label={"Hide #{section.name} section"}
              title="Hide section"
            >
              <span class="hero-eye-slash size-3.5"></span>
            </button>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="channel-section-drag-handle"
              aria-label={"Reorder #{section.name} section"}
              tabindex="-1"
              draggable="true"
            >
              ☰
            </button>
          </div>
          <%!-- Admin-edit (Stage 6): compact recolor palette — the 5 scope
               tokens ARE the palette (no free-form color picker). Each swatch
               posts `recolor_section_default` with the section id + token; the
               active token is marked so the admin sees the current color. The
               server whitelist-validates the token and re-checks fabrikam_admin?
               before writing `channel_sections.color`. --%>
          <div
            :if={@sidebar_admin_edit}
            class="channel-section-palette"
            role="group"
            aria-label={"Set color for #{section.name} section"}
          >
            <button
              :for={token <- ~w(fabrikam soylent wayne-tech sxi paragon)}
              type="button"
              phx-click="recolor_section_default"
              phx-value-section_id={section.id}
              phx-value-color={token}
              class={[
                "channel-section-swatch",
                "channel-section-swatch--#{token}",
                section.color == token && "channel-section-swatch--active"
              ]}
              aria-pressed={to_string(section.color == token)}
              aria-label={"Color: #{token}"}
              title={token}
            >
            </button>
          </div>
          <%= if section_channels == [] do %>
            <p class="channel-section-empty">
              No channels yet — channels in this org appear here.
            </p>
          <% else %>
            <div
              :for={{space, idx} <- Enum.with_index(section_channels)}
              class={[
                "channel-row-wrap",
                (@sidebar_edit || @sidebar_admin_edit) && "channel-row-wrap--editing",
                @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row-wrap--active"
              ]}
              data-channel-id={space.id}
              data-section-id={section.id}
            >
              <%!-- Grab handle (Stage 5 personal-edit + Stage 6 admin-edit).
                   This span — not the row-wrap — carries draggable so it is the
                   HTML5 drag SOURCE node: dragstart's e.target is then this span,
                   so the ChannelMembershipDrag hook's `.channel-row-grab` gate
                   matches (mirroring SectionReorder, whose handle is the source
                   too). A click on the row link still navigates because the link
                   isn't draggable. tabindex=-1 because the keyboard alternative
                   is the Up/Down buttons (personal-edit only). Rendered in EITHER
                   edit mode — in personal-edit the drop pushes `channel_moved`
                   (per-user), in admin-edit it pushes `channel_reassigned`
                   (global org_id); the hook reads `data-admin-edit` to decide. --%>
              <span
                :if={@sidebar_edit || @sidebar_admin_edit}
                class="channel-row-grab"
                aria-hidden="true"
                title={
                  if @sidebar_admin_edit,
                    do: "Drag to reassign for everyone",
                    else: "Drag to move"
                }
                draggable="true"
              >
                ⠿
              </span>
              <.link
                navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug || space.id}"}
                class={[
                  "channel-row",
                  @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id && "channel-row--active"
                ]}
              >
                <span class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
                <span class="truncate flex-1">{space.name}</span>
                <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
                  <span class="channel-row-unread-pill">
                    {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
                  </span>
                <% end %>
              </.link>
              <%!-- Keyboard move controls (Stage 5, edit mode only — WCAG
                   2.1.1 keyboard alternative to drag). Each posts the same
                   `move_channel` event the keyboard path shares with drag's
                   `channel_moved` persistence. Up is disabled on the first
                   row, Down on the last, so focus can't trigger a no-op
                   that reads as broken. --%>
              <span :if={@sidebar_edit} class="channel-row-move-controls">
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-row-move-button"
                  phx-click="move_channel"
                  phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                  phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                  phx-value-direction="up"
                  disabled={idx == 0}
                  aria-label={"Move ##{space.name} up"}
                  title="Move up"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-up size-3"></span>
                </button>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="channel-row-move-button"
                  phx-click="move_channel"
                  phx-value-channel_id={space.id}
                  phx-value-section_id={section.id}
                  phx-value-direction="down"
                  disabled={idx == length(section_channels) - 1}
                  aria-label={"Move ##{space.name} down"}
                  title="Move down"
                >
                  <span class="hero-chevron-down size-3"></span>
                </button>
              </span>
              <%!-- Per-channel hide affordance (chat sidebar v3 Stage 2). Sub-org
                   rows ONLY (NOT Pinned, NOT DMs). Rendered as a SIBLING of the
                   row link — never a child — so its click reaches LiveView's
                   window-level `phx-click` listener. A <button> nested in the
                   <a> is invalid HTML, and the old anti-navigation
                   stopPropagation guard there also swallowed the hide event
                   (LiveView binds click on `window` in the bubble phase, so
                   stopPropagation killed it). Outside the anchor, clicking the
                   button can't trigger navigation, so no propagation guard is
                   needed. Revealed on wrapper :hover OR :focus-within for
                   keyboard reach (WCAG 2.1.1). --%>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="channel-row-hide-button"
                phx-click="hide_channel"
                phx-value-id={space.id}
                aria-label={"Hide ##{space.name}"}
                title="Hide channel"
              >
                <span class="hero-eye-slash size-3.5"></span>
              </button>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </section>
      </div>

      <%!-- Reset to default layout (chat sidebar Stage 5, edit mode only).
           Clears all three per-user override keys (section order, channel
           placement, hidden sections) so the rail returns to the org default
           — the only way to un-hide a section hidden via the per-section
           control above. --%>
      <button
        :if={@sidebar_edit}
        type="button"
        phx-click="reset_sidebar"
        class="channel-reset-layout-button"
        aria-label="Reset to default layout"
      >
        <span class="hero-arrow-path size-4"></span>
        <span>Reset to default layout</span>
      </button>

      <%!-- Brand-new-user empty state — surfaces when the user has no
           channels AND no DMs at all. The sub-org headers above still
           render (with their own empty-state hints), but a separate
           top-level invite chip keeps the "Welcome to Suite" message
           from Stage 1 visible. --%>
      <.empty_state
        :if={@channels == [] and @dm_conversations == []}
        variant={:conversational}
      >
        <:system_message>— no spaces yet —</:system_message>
        <:body>Welcome to Suite. To get started, create a space or connect your agent.</:body>
        <:chips label="+ Create a space" event="new_channel_open" />
        <:chips label="+ Connect an agent" event={JS.navigate(~p"/control")} />
      </.empty_state>
    </nav>

    <%!-- Undo toast — ephemeral 4-second affordance shown after a hide
         (Stage 3 v3 follow-up per Marlowe's 2026-05-29 review). Lives as
         an IN-FLOW `flex-shrink-0` sibling between the scrolling `<nav>`
         (`flex-1`) above and the pinned "+ New channel" button below.
         When the toast appears, the `flex-1` scroll nav absorbs its
         height by shrinking — so "+ New channel" stays exactly where it
         is, the drawer stays exactly where it is, and the toast doesn't
         overlap any content. Trades a soft scroll-area compression for
         stable pinned chrome (the right exchange — overlap with content
         is the actual user complaint; transient scroll compression is
         the standard chat-rail behavior, same way Slack/Discord handle
         compose-area system notes).

         role=status + aria-live=polite (NOT assertive) — hiding a
         channel is non-destructive (nothing deleted, only user-filtered)
         so a polite announcement is the right WCAG choice. The Undo
         button shares its handler with the drawer's Show buttons via
         do_unhide/2 in the LiveView, so the round-trip is identical
         regardless of which way the user reverses the hide. Auto-clears
         via a Process.send_after → handle_info({:clear_undo_toast,
         space_id}) pair scheduled by the hide_channel handler. --%>
    <div
      :if={@undo_toast}
      role="status"
      aria-live="polite"
      class="channel-undo-toast"
    >
      <span class="channel-undo-toast-message">
        Hidden <span class="font-medium">#{@undo_toast.name}</span>
      </span>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="channel-undo-toast-button"
        phx-click="undo_hide"
        phx-value-id={@undo_toast.space_id}
      >
        Undo
      </button>
    </div>

    <%!-- "+ New channel" — pinned rail chrome (Stage 3 v3 follow-up per
         Marlowe's review). Lives as an UNCONDITIONAL `flex-shrink-0` sibling
         of `<nav>` and the conditional bottom-region wrapper, so its
         visual position never drifts based on channel count OR on whether
         the undo toast / hidden drawer happens to be showing. The wrapper
         was deliberately NOT merged into the bottom-region's `:if` block —
         doing so would yank the button out of view whenever both toast
         and drawer are absent, reintroducing the "position depends on
         state" bug. Visual divider above is a top border using the same
         `border-base-content/10` token the aside itself uses, so the
         rail's separator language stays consistent. Reuses the
         channel-row hover/text vocabulary so the button rhymes visually
         with the section rows above. --%>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click="new_channel_open"
      aria-label="New channel"
      class="flex-shrink-0 flex items-center gap-2 w-full border-t border-base-content/10 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors"
    >
      <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
      <span>New channel</span>
    </button>

    <%!-- Bottom region (Stage 3 v3): hosts the global "N hidden channels"
         drawer ONLY. Silent at N=0 — the wrapper is :if-gated to
         `hidden_count > 0` so it disappears entirely when the user has
         no hidden channels, keeping the sidebar foot empty in the clean
         state. The undo toast used to live here too but moved up to its
         own in-flow position above "+ New channel" — keeps pinned chrome
         (+ New channel, drawer trigger) stable when a hide fires, since
         the scroll-nav (flex-1) absorbs the toast's height instead. --%>
    <% hidden_count =
      @channel_sections.hidden_sub_orgs
      |> Map.values()
      |> Enum.map(&length/1)
      |> Enum.sum() %>
    <div
      :if={hidden_count > 0}
      class="flex-shrink-0 border-t border-base-content/10 px-2 py-2"
    >
      <%!-- Global "N hidden channels" drawer (Option B per Marlowe's v3
           review). One quiet row at the rail's foot — silent at N=0 —
           expanding upward into a scrollable grouped list. The panel
           ALWAYS renders so the max-height CSS transition animates in
           and out smoothly; the `--open` modifier on the wrapper drives
           the transition. Internal scroll caps the panel at min(50vh,
           360px) so it can't claim more than half the sidebar at very
           high hidden counts. Each Show button shares the unhide_channel
           handler with the (now-removed) v2 inline list, so behavior is
           identical to v2 — only the trigger surface changed. --%>
      <div
        :if={hidden_count > 0}
        class={[
          "channel-hidden-drawer",
          @hidden_drawer_open && "channel-hidden-drawer--open"
        ]}
      >
        <div
          id="hidden-drawer-panel"
          class="channel-hidden-drawer-panel"
          aria-hidden={if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "false", else: "true"}
        >
          <%= for {bucket, hidden_channels} <- @channel_sections.hidden_sub_orgs,
                  hidden_channels != [] do %>
            <div class="channel-hidden-drawer-group">
              <div class="channel-hidden-drawer-group-label">
                <.scope_pill scope={sub_org_scope_atom(bucket)} clickable={false} />
              </div>
              <ul class="channel-hidden-drawer-group-list">
                <li
                  :for={space <- hidden_channels}
                  class="channel-hidden-drawer-item"
                >
                  <span class="text-base-content/40">#</span>
                  <span class="truncate flex-1">{space.name}</span>
                  <button
                    type="button"
                    class="channel-hidden-drawer-show"
                    phx-click="unhide_channel"
                    phx-value-id={space.id}
                    aria-label={"Show ##{space.name}"}
                  >
                    Show
                  </button>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="channel-hidden-drawer-trigger"
          phx-click="toggle_hidden_drawer"
          aria-expanded={if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "true", else: "false"}
          aria-controls="hidden-drawer-panel"
          aria-label={
            if @hidden_drawer_open,
              do: "Collapse hidden channels",
              else: "Show #{hidden_count} hidden channels"
          }
        >
          <span class="flex-1 text-left">
            {hidden_count} hidden {if hidden_count == 1, do: "channel", else: "channels"}
          </span>
          <span class="channel-hidden-drawer-caret">
            {if @hidden_drawer_open, do: "▾", else: "▴"}
          </span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <%!-- Drag handle for sidebar resize --%>
    <div
      class="absolute right-0 inset-y-0 w-1 cursor-col-resize hover:bg-primary/40 active:bg-primary/60 transition-colors z-10"
      aria-hidden="true"
    />
  </aside>

  <%!-- Mobile channel browser overlay — suppressed when embedded. --%>
  <%= if @mobile_browser_open and !@embedded do %>
    <div class="fixed inset-0 z-40 flex flex-col bg-base-100 lg:hidden safe-area-x">
      <header class="flex h-12 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b border-base-300 px-4 safe-area-top">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold">Conversations</p>
        <button
          phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
          class="flex items-center justify-center size-10 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content"
          aria-label="Close"
        >
          <span class="hero-x-mark size-5"></span>
        </button>
      </header>

      <nav class="flex-1 overflow-y-auto py-2">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-1">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
            Channels
          </p>
          <button
            phx-click={JS.push("new_channel_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
            class="flex items-center justify-center size-11 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-primary"
            aria-label="New channel"
            title="New channel"
          >
            <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <.link
          :for={space <- @channels}
          navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug}"}
          phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
            "hover:bg-base-200",
            @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
              "bg-base-200 text-primary font-semibold"
          ]}
        >
          <span class="text-base-content/40 text-lg">#</span>
          <span class="truncate flex-1">{space.name}</span>
          <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
            <span class="ml-1 flex-shrink-0 min-w-[1.125rem] h-[1.125rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.6rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center px-1 leading-none">
              {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            </span>
          <% end %>
        </.link>

        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-1 mt-2">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
            Direct Messages
          </p>
          <button
            phx-click={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
            class="flex items-center justify-center size-11 rounded-lg text-base-content/60 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-primary"
            aria-label="New conversation"
            title="New conversation"
          >
            <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <.link
          :for={space <- @dm_conversations}
          navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug || space.id}"}
          phx-click="close_mobile_browser"
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 text-sm transition-colors",
            "hover:bg-base-200",
            @active_space && @active_space.id == space.id &&
              "bg-base-200 text-primary font-semibold"
          ]}
        >
          <span class="truncate flex-1">{sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}</span>
          <%= if unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0)) do %>
            <span class="ml-1 flex-shrink-0 min-w-[1.125rem] h-[1.125rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.6rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center px-1 leading-none">
              {unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            </span>
          <% end %>
        </.link>

        <%!-- Empty state per docs/design-system/03-voice.md §5.1 — mobile
             combined view (no channels AND no DMs). Chip event is a JS
             chain so opening the new-conversation flow also closes the
             mobile browser overlay. --%>
        <.empty_state
          :if={@channels == [] and @dm_conversations == []}
          variant={:conversational}
        >
          <:system_message>— no conversations yet —</:system_message>
          <:body>
            Start your first conversation. Pick a channel or DM someone in your space.
          </:body>
          <:chips
            label="+ Start your first conversation"
            event={JS.push("new_conversation_open") |> JS.push("close_mobile_browser")}
          />
        </.empty_state>
      </nav>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex flex-1 overflow-hidden min-w-0 min-h-0">
    <div
      id="chat-drop-zone"
      phx-hook="DragDropUpload"
      class="flex flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden min-w-0 min-h-0"
    >
      <header
        :if={@active_space && !@embedded}
        class="flex h-12 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b border-base-content/10 px-5"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden">
          <%!-- Mobile: static channel name. Channel switching now happens via the
               pills strip below the header (Refined Option A — Marlowe approval
               2026-05-10). The previous tap-channel-name-to-open-browser flow
               was confusing with the shell's hamburger menu — both opened
               drawers, so users could tap one when they meant the other. The
               pills strip makes channel switching 1-tap and removes the
               dual-affordance ambiguity. The overflow magnifying-glass icon at
               the right of the strip still opens the full channel browser
               (this template's @mobile_browser_open overlay) for the long-tail
               jump-to-channel case. --%>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden lg:hidden">
            <span :if={@active_space.kind == "channel"} class="text-base-content/50">#</span>
            <span class="truncate font-semibold">
              {space_header_name(@active_space, @space_participants, @user_id)}
            </span>
          </div>
          <%!-- Desktop: static title --%>
          <span class="hidden lg:flex items-center gap-2 overflow-hidden">
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "channel"}
              class="text-base-content/50 text-lg font-bold"
            >
              #
            </span>
            <span class="truncate font-bold text-base">
              {space_header_name(@active_space, @space_participants, @user_id)}
            </span>
            <%!-- Prominent chat-header scope-pill (chat plan v2 Stage 4).
                 Only rendered for channels (DMs/groups have no scope). The
                 wrapper class drives the larger-size visual variant; the
                 inner pill remains clickable and pushes the `scope_filter`
                 event with the channel's scope. Active state is implied
                 from `@scope_filter` so a clicked-again pill reads as the
                 currently-selected filter. --%>
            <% header_scope = PlatformWeb.ChatLive.space_scope_atom(@active_space) %>
            <span :if={header_scope} class="chat-header-scope-pill">
              <.scope_pill
                scope={header_scope}
                clickable={true}
                active={@scope_filter == header_scope}
              />
            </span>
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "channel" && @active_space.topic}
              class="truncate text-xs text-base-content/40"
            >
              — {@active_space.topic}
            </span>
            <span
              :if={@active_space.kind == "group"}
              class="text-xs text-base-content/40"
            >
              — {length(Enum.filter(@space_participants, &is_nil(&1.left_at)))} members
            </span>
          </span>

          <%!-- Promote to channel button for groups --%>
          <form
            :if={@active_space.kind == "group" && !@active_space.is_direct}
            id="promote-to-channel-form"
            phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
            phx-submit="promote_to_channel"
            class="hidden lg:flex items-center gap-1 ml-2"
          >
            <input
              name="name"
              type="text"
              placeholder="Channel name…"
              class="input input-bordered input-xs w-32"
              required
            />
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost">
              Convert to Channel
            </button>
          </form>
        </div>

        <%!-- Join Meeting button --%>
        <button
          :if={@meetings_enabled && !@in_meeting}
          phx-click="meeting_join"
          class="flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2 py-1 rounded-lg text-xs font-medium text-base-content/60 hover:text-primary hover:bg-primary/10 transition-colors"
          title="Start or join a meeting in this space"
        >
          <span class="hero-video-camera size-4"></span>
          <span class="hidden md:inline">Meet</span>
        </button>

        <div class="flex flex-shrink-0 items-center gap-3 text-xs text-base-content/50">
          <.form
            for={@search_form}
            id="chat-search-form"
            phx-change="search_submit"
            phx-submit="search_submit"
            class="hidden md:block"
          >
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <.input
                field={@search_form[:query]}
                type="text"
                placeholder="Search messages…"
                autocomplete="off"
                phx-debounce="250"
                class="input input-bordered input-sm w-64 text-sm"
              />

              <button
                :if={present?(@search_query)}
                type="button"
                phx-click="search_clear"
                class="rounded px-2 py-1 text-xs hover:bg-base-300"
              >
                Clear
              </button>
            </div>
          </.form>

          <button
            :if={@canvases != []}
            phx-click="canvas_panel_toggle"
            class={[
              "flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300",
              @show_canvases && "!bg-base-300 !text-primary"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="hero-puzzle-piece size-4"></span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">{length(@canvases)}</span>
          </button>

          <button
            :if={@pins != []}
            phx-click="pin_panel_toggle"
            class={[
              "flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300",
              @show_pins && "!bg-base-300 !text-primary"
            ]}
          >
            <span class="hero-bookmark-solid size-4"></span>
            <span>{length(@pins)} pinned</span>
          </button>

          <%!-- Active agent indicator --%>
          <span
            :if={@active_agent_participant_id != nil}
            class="flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-success"
          >
            <span>🟢</span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">Talking to {@active_agent_name || "Agent"}</span>
            <button
              phx-click="active_agent_clear"
              class="ml-1 text-base-content/40 hover:text-error transition-colors"
              title="Clear active agent"
            >
              <span class="hero-x-mark size-3"></span>
            </button>
          </span>
          <span
            :if={
              @active_agent_participant_id == nil && @active_space.watch_enabled &&
                (@agent_presence[:joined?] || @has_agent_participant)
            }
            class="flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-success/60"
          >
            <span>🟢</span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">
              {PresenceHooks.primary_agent_label(@active_space, @space_participants)} listening
            </span>
          </span>

          <%!-- Watch toggle (hidden for DM spaces — always ON) --%>
          <button
            :if={
              (@agent_presence[:joined?] || @has_agent_participant) && @active_space.kind != "dm"
            }
            phx-click="toggle_watch"
            class={[
              "flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300",
              !@active_space.watch_enabled && "!bg-warning/20 !text-warning"
            ]}
            title={
              if @active_space.watch_enabled,
                do: "Disable watch — agent won't auto-respond",
                else: "Enable watch — agent will auto-respond"
            }
          >
            <span class={[
              "size-4",
              if(@active_space.watch_enabled, do: "hero-eye", else: "hero-eye-slash")
            ]}>
            </span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">
              {if @active_space.watch_enabled, do: "watching", else: "paused"}
            </span>
          </button>

          <button
            phx-click="settings_open"
            class="flex items-center gap-1 rounded px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content transition-colors hover:bg-base-300"
            title="Space settings"
          >
            <span class="hero-cog-6-tooth size-4"></span>
            <span class="hidden md:inline">settings</span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </header>

      <%!-- Mobile-only channel pills strip — Refined Option A nav (Marlowe approval 2026-05-10).
           Replaces the previous tap-channel-name-to-open-browser flow. Renders @channels
           as horizontally-scrollable pills with the active channel highlighted. The
           overflow magnifying-glass icon at the end opens the existing
           @mobile_browser_open overlay (which has the full channel + DM list and is
           the long-tail jump-to-channel surface). 1-tap channel switching for the
           pills shown; 2-tap (overflow → search/select) for the long tail.

           Pinning is NOT in this Stage 1A — channels appear in the existing order
           (alphabetical via Chat.list_spaces). A follow-up Stage 1B will add
           localStorage-backed pinning + long-press to pin/unpin. --%>
      <nav
        :if={@active_space && !@embedded}
        class="lg:hidden flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto px-4 py-2 border-b border-base-content/10"
        style="scrollbar-width: none; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;"
        aria-label="Channel switcher"
      >
        <%!-- Search/jump button anchored at the LEFT of the pills strip
             (Rowan request, Marlowe approval 2026-05-11). Sticks to the left
             edge so it stays in reach even as the channel pills overflow
             horizontally and scroll. --%>
        <button
          phx-click="toggle_mobile_browser"
          class="flex items-center justify-center w-9 h-9 rounded-full shrink-0 bg-base-200 border border-base-content/10 text-base-content/50 hover:text-primary hover:bg-base-300 transition-colors sticky left-0 z-10"
          aria-label="Search channels and direct messages"
          title="Search channels and DMs"
        >
          <span class="hero-magnifying-glass size-4"></span>
        </button>

        <.link
          :for={space <- @channels}
          navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug}"}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0 transition-all",
            "active:scale-[0.97] ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]",
            if @active_space.id == space.id do
              "bg-primary text-primary-content shadow-[0_0_16px_oklch(0.78_0.14_207_/_0.18)]"
            else
              "bg-base-200 text-base-content/70 border border-base-content/10 hover:bg-base-300"
            end
          ]}
        >
          <span class={[
            if(@active_space.id == space.id,
              do: "text-primary-content/80",
              else: "text-base-content/40"
            )
          ]}>#</span>{space.name}<span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >{unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}</span>
        </.link>

        <%!-- DM pills (after channels, no divider for now to keep mobile compact) --%>
        <.link
          :for={space <- @dm_conversations}
          navigate={~p"/chat/#{space.slug || space.id}"}
          class={[
            "flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-medium shrink-0 transition-all",
            "active:scale-[0.97] ease-[cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)]",
            if @active_space.id == space.id do
              "bg-primary text-primary-content shadow-[0_0_16px_oklch(0.78_0.14_207_/_0.18)]"
            else
              "bg-base-200 text-base-content/70 border border-base-content/10 hover:bg-base-300"
            end
          ]}
        >
          {sidebar_display_name(space, @user_id)}<span
            :if={unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-w-[18px] h-[18px] rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold tabular-nums bg-primary text-primary-content border border-base-100"
          >{unread_label(Map.get(@unread_counts, space.id, 0))}</span>
        </.link>
      </nav>

      <div
        :if={present?(@search_query)}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-3"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              Search Results
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
              “{@search_query}” · {length(@search_results)} match{if length(@search_results) == 1,
                do: "",
                else: "es"}
            </p>
          </div>

          <button phx-click="search_clear" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs">
            Clear
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-3 space-y-2">
          <button
            :for={result <- @search_results}
            type="button"
            phx-click="search_open_result"
            phx-value-message-id={result.id}
            class="block w-full rounded-xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3 py-2 text-left transition-colors hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-base-100/80"
          >
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              <span>{PresenceHooks.sender_name(@participants_map, result.participant_id)}</span>
              <.local_time
                id={"search-time-#{result.id}"}
                timestamp={result.inserted_at}
              />
              <span
                :if={is_binary(result.thread_id)}
                class="rounded-full bg-base-300 px-2 py-0.5 normal-case tracking-normal text-[10px]"
              >
                Thread
              </span>
              <span
                :if={result.search_rank}
                class="font-mono normal-case tracking-normal text-[10px] text-base-content/40"
              >
                rank {Float.round(result.search_rank, 3)}
              </span>
            </div>

            <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-6 text-base-content">
              {search_headline(result)}
            </p>
          </button>

          <%!-- Empty state per docs/design-system/03-voice.md §5.5 — search
               no-results uses :standard with the magnifying-glass icon. --%>
          <.empty_state
            :if={@search_results == [] and present?(@search_query)}
            variant={:standard}
            icon_name="hero-magnifying-glass"
          >
            <:title>No matches</:title>
            <:body>No messages match "{@search_query}".</:body>
            <:actions>
              <button
                type="button"
                phx-click="search_clear"
                class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm w-full"
              >
                Clear search
              </button>
            </:actions>
          </.empty_state>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        :if={@show_pins && @pins != []}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-2"
      >
        <p class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
          Pinned Messages
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1 max-h-40 overflow-y-auto">
          <div
            :for={pin <- @pins}
            class="flex items-center justify-between rounded bg-base-100 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm"
          >
            <span class="truncate text-base-content/70 text-xs">
              <span class="hero-bookmark-solid size-3 inline-block align-text-bottom"></span>
              pinned message
              <span class="font-mono text-base-content/40 text-[10px]">
                {String.slice(pin.message_id, 0, 8)}…
              </span>
            </span>
            <button
              phx-click="pin_toggle"
              phx-value-message-id={pin.message_id}
              phx-value-space-id={pin.space_id}
              class="ml-2 text-xs text-base-content/40 hover:text-error"
            >
              Unpin
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div
        :if={@show_canvases}
        class="border-b border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-3"
      >
        <div class="grid gap-3 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_320px]">
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
              Live Canvases
            </p>

            <button
              :for={canvas <- @canvases}
              type="button"
              phx-click="canvas_open"
              phx-value-canvas-id={canvas.id}
              class={[
                "flex w-full items-center justify-between rounded-xl border px-3 py-2 text-left transition-colors",
                "border-base-300 bg-base-100 hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-base-100/80",
                @active_canvas && @active_canvas.id == canvas.id && "border-primary bg-primary/5"
              ]}
            >
              <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold text-base-content">
                  {canvas.title || CanvasHooks.humanize_kind(canvas)}
                </p>
                <p class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                  {CanvasHooks.humanize_kind(canvas)}
                </p>
              </div>

              <span class="ml-3 rounded-full bg-base-300 px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] text-base-content/60">
                Open
              </span>
            </button>

            <div
              :if={@canvases == []}
              class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-base-300 bg-base-100 px-3 py-4 text-sm text-base-content/50"
            >
              No canvases yet. Create one to collaborate live in this channel.
            </div>
          </div>

          <.form
            for={@new_canvas_form}
            id="new-canvas-form"
            phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
            phx-submit="canvas_create"
            class="space-y-3 rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-4"
          >
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-base-content">New canvas</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50">
                Creates a canvas and posts a linked canvas message.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-1.5">
              <label class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/50">
                Title
              </label>
              <input
                type="text"
                name="canvas[title]"
                value={@new_canvas_form[:title].value || ""}
                placeholder="Sprint planning board"
                class="input input-bordered w-full"
              />
            </div>

            <button
              type="submit"
              class="btn btn-neutral w-full"
              disabled={is_nil(@current_participant)}
            >
              Create canvas
            </button>
          </.form>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="inline-focus-listener" phx-hook="InlineFocus" class="hidden"></div>
      <%!-- min-h-0 is the load-bearing class here: without it, flex items
           default to `min-height: auto` which means the message list
           refuses to shrink below its intrinsic content height. With 80+
           messages that intrinsic height blows past the viewport and
           pushes the composer + bottom-tab nav off-screen on iOS Safari /
           PWA standalone. overscroll-contain stops rubber-band gestures
           from reaching the document scroller (defence-in-depth: app.css
           already has `overscroll-behavior: none` on body, but iOS WebKit
           respects the per-scroller setting more reliably than the
           ancestor chain). --%>
      <%!-- Outer scroll wrapper for infinite scroll (task 019e18fc Stage
           3). The sentinels live inside this wrapper as siblings of
           #message-list — that way they're inside the scroll viewport
           and the InfiniteScroll IntersectionObserver fires when the
           user scrolls them into view. #message-list itself becomes a
           non-scrolling flex column inside the wrapper. Overflow +
           overscroll moved from #message-list to here. --%>
      <div
        id="chat-message-scroller"
        data-scroll-container
        class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto overflow-x-hidden overscroll-contain bg-base-100"
      >
        <%!-- Top sentinel: fires `load_older_messages` when visible AND
             :has_more_older is true. --%>
        <div
          :if={@has_more_older}
          id="chat-scroll-sentinel-top"
          phx-hook="InfiniteScroll"
          data-direction="older"
          data-loading={if @loading_older, do: "true"}
          class="flex justify-center py-2 text-xs text-base-content/40"
        >
          <span :if={@loading_older} class="hero-arrow-path size-3 animate-spin"></span>
          <span :if={!@loading_older}>Loading older messages…</span>
        </div>

        <div
          id="message-list"
          class="px-5 py-4 flex flex-col space-y-1"
          phx-update="stream"
          phx-hook="ScrollToBottom"
        >
          <.chat_message
            :for={{dom_id, msg} <- @streams.messages}
            :if={is_nil(msg.deleted_at)}
            dom_id={dom_id}
            msg={msg}
            current_participant={@current_participant}
            agent_participant_ids={@agent_participant_ids}
            agent_colors_map={@agent_colors_map}
            participants_map={@participants_map}
            quick_emojis={@quick_emojis}
            pinned_message_ids={@pinned_message_ids}
            highlighted_message_id={@highlighted_message_id}
            canvases_by_id={@canvases_by_id}
            attachments_map={@attachments_map}
            thread_previews={@thread_previews}
            expanded_threads={@expanded_threads}
            inline_thread_messages={@inline_thread_messages}
            mention_suggestions={@mention_suggestions}
            mention_source={@mention_source}
            editing_message_id={@editing_message_id}
          />
        </div>

        <%!-- Bottom sentinel: fires `load_newer_messages` when visible AND
             :newest_evicted? is true. Only renders after the live tail
             has been evicted by a prepend (Stage 2's prune logic). --%>
        <div
          :if={@newest_evicted?}
          id="chat-scroll-sentinel-bottom"
          phx-hook="InfiniteScroll"
          data-direction="newer"
          data-loading={if @loading_newer, do: "true"}
          class="flex justify-center py-2 text-xs text-base-content/40"
        >
          <span :if={@loading_newer} class="hero-arrow-path size-3 animate-spin"></span>
          <span :if={!@loading_newer}>Loading newer messages…</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%!-- Streaming reply bubbles --%>
      <div
        :for={{chunk_id, entry} <- @streaming_replies}
        :if={entry.text != nil and entry.text != ""}
        id={"streaming-#{chunk_id}"}
        class="flex-shrink-0 px-5 pb-2 msg-agent"
        style={
          "--agent-accent: #{Map.get(@agent_colors_map, entry.participant_id, Platform.Agents.ColorPalette.default_accent())};"
        }
      >
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <div class="flex size-7 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-base-300 text-xs font-medium msg-agent-avatar">
            {PresenceHooks.avatar_initial(@participants_map, entry.participant_id)}
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="text-xs font-medium mb-0.5 msg-agent-name">
              {PresenceHooks.sender_name(@participants_map, entry.participant_id)}
            </div>
            <div
              class="text-sm text-base-content/80 border-l-2 pl-3"
              style="border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--agent-accent, oklch(82% 0.12 207)) 30%, transparent);"
            >
              {entry.text}<span
                class="inline-block w-1.5 h-4 animate-pulse ml-0.5 align-middle rounded-sm"
                style="background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--agent-accent, oklch(82% 0.12 207)) 50%, transparent);"
              ></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%!-- Typing indicator --%>
      <div
        :if={not MapSet.equal?(@agent_typing_pids, MapSet.new()) and @streaming_replies == %{}}
        class="flex-shrink-0 px-5 pb-1 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-base-content/50"
      >
        <span class="flex gap-0.5 items-center">
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 0ms"
          >
          </span>
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 150ms"
          >
          </span>
          <span
            class="inline-block size-1.5 rounded-full bg-base-content/40 animate-bounce"
            style="animation-delay: 300ms"
          >
          </span>
        </span>
        <span>
          {PresenceHooks.thinking_label(@agent_typing_pids, @participants_map)} is thinking…
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="flex-shrink-0 compose-input-area safe-area-bottom">
        <.form
          :if={@active_space}
          for={@compose_form}
          id="compose-form"
          phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
          phx-submit="send_message"
          phx-change="compose_changed"
          class="flex flex-col gap-2"
        >
          <%!-- @mention autocomplete dropdown --%>
          <div
            :if={@mention_suggestions != [] && @mention_source == "compose-form"}
            class="relative"
          >
            <div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 z-50 w-64 rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 shadow-lg overflow-hidden">
              <div class="py-1">
                <button
                  :for={{suggestion, idx} <- Enum.with_index(@mention_suggestions)}
                  type="button"
                  data-mention-suggestion={if idx == 0, do: "first"}
                  phx-click={
                    JS.dispatch("chat:insert-mention",
                      to: "##{@compose_form[:text].id}",
                      detail: %{name: suggestion.name}
                    )
                  }
                  class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 text-sm hover:bg-base-200 text-left transition-colors"
                >
                  <%= if suggestion.participant_type == "agent" do %>
                    <div class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content flex items-center justify-center text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0">
                      {suggestion
                      |> Map.get(:name)
                      |> String.trim()
                      |> String.first()
                      |> String.upcase()}
                    </div>
                  <% else %>
                    <.human_avatar
                      name={suggestion.name}
                      avatar_url={suggestion.avatar_url}
                      seed={suggestion.avatar_seed}
                      size="sm"
                      class="flex-shrink-0"
                    />
                  <% end %>
                  <span class="flex-1 truncate font-medium">
                    {suggestion.name}
                  </span>
                  <span class={[
                    "rounded-full px-1.5 py-0.5 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider",
                    suggestion.participant_type == "agent" && "bg-primary/10 text-primary",
                    suggestion.participant_type != "agent" && "bg-base-300 text-base-content/50"
                  ]}>
                    {suggestion.participant_type}
                  </span>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%!-- Pill-shaped compose bar --%>
          <div class="compose-pill-bar">
            <button
              type="button"
              id="compose-attach-button"
              phx-hook="UploadButton"
              phx-click="upload_dialog_open"
              class="compose-pill-attach cursor-pointer text-base-content/50 hover:bg-base-300/50 transition-colors"
              title="Attach files"
            >
              <span class="hero-plus size-5"></span>
            </button>

            <textarea
              name="compose[text]"
              id={@compose_form[:text].id}
              data-draft-key={if @active_space, do: "chat-draft:" <> @active_space.id, else: nil}
              placeholder={"Message ##{(@active_space && @active_space.name) || ""}"}
              autocomplete="off"
              rows="1"
              class="min-w-0 flex-1 text-sm resize-none"
              style="line-height:1.5;padding:4px 0;min-height:28px;max-height:200px;overflow-y:auto;field-sizing:content"
              phx-hook="ComposeInput"
            >{Phoenix.HTML.Form.normalize_value("text", @compose_form[:text].value)}</textarea>

            <button
              type="submit"
              class="compose-pill-send"
              disabled={is_nil(@current_participant) or composer_empty?(@compose_form)}
              aria-label="Send message"
              title="Send"
            >
              <span class="hero-paper-airplane size-4 -rotate-45"></span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p
            :for={error <- upload_errors(@uploads.attachments)}
            class="text-xs text-error"
          >
            {upload_error_to_string(error)}
          </p>

          <div :for={entry <- @uploads.attachments.entries}>
            <p
              :for={error <- upload_errors(@uploads.attachments, entry)}
              class="text-xs text-error"
            >
              {entry.client_name}: {upload_error_to_string(error)}
            </p>
          </div>
        </.form>

        <%!-- Always-present upload submission form. Lives OUTSIDE #compose-form
             (HTML forbids nested forms) so the modal's Send button + textarea
             can target it via the HTML5 `form="upload-send-form"` attribute.
             The form is rendered unconditionally so:
               (a) `inputEl.form` resolves on first paste (no chicken-and-egg
                   with `:if={entries != []}` form-rendering).
               (b) LiveView's `pushInput` → `pushFormSubmit` always finds the
                   form to serialize when the user submits.
             The hidden file input (`live_file_input`) is the form's only
             direct child; visible UI for caption + Send lives inside the
             modal panel and links back to this form via `form=...`. --%>
        <form
          :if={@active_space}
          id="upload-send-form"
          phx-hook="ButtonLoading"
          phx-submit="upload_send"
          phx-change="upload_caption_change"
          class="hidden"
        >
          <.live_file_input upload={@uploads.attachments} class="sr-only" />
        </form>

        <p :if={is_nil(@current_participant) && @active_space} class="mt-1 text-xs text-error">
          Unable to join space — messages are read-only.
        </p>
      </div>

      <.upload_dialog
        open={@upload_dialog_open}
        active_space={@active_space}
        uploads={@uploads}
        caption={@upload_caption}
        tagged_agents={@upload_tagged_agents}
      />
    </div>

    <.canvas_overlay
      canvas={@active_canvas}
      show_versions_panel={@show_versions_panel}
      canvas_versions={@canvas_versions}
      restore_confirm_revision={@restore_confirm_revision}
    />

    <%!-- Embedded surfaces (e.g. inside MeetingLive) leave the meeting
         mini-bar to the parent — the parent already owns the live
         meeting state. Skip the panel here to avoid a double mini-bar. --%>
    <.meeting_panel
      :if={!@embedded}
      in_meeting={@in_meeting}
      active_space={@active_space}
      mic_enabled={@mic_enabled}
      camera_enabled={@camera_enabled}
      screen_share_enabled={@screen_share_enabled}
      meeting_participants={@meeting_participants}
    />
  </div>
</div>

<%!-- Standalone-only modals: settings, new-channel, new-conversation.
     The embedded surface (e.g. meeting chat panel) scopes to one space
     and has no affordances to open these, so the components are skipped
     to keep the embed lean. --%>
<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded}
  module={SettingsComponent}
  id="chat-settings"
  open={@show_settings}
  space={@active_space}
/>

<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded}
  module={NewChannelComponent}
  id="chat-new-channel"
  open={@show_new_channel_modal}
/>

<.live_component
  :if={!@embedded}
  module={NewConversationComponent}
  id="chat-new-conversation"
  open={@show_new_conversation_modal}
  user_id={@user_id}
/>

<%!--
  Reaction picker — bottom sheet on mobile, centered modal on desktop.
  Shape is controlled by the `reaction-picker` CSS class: below the
  640px breakpoint the panel slides up from the bottom with safe-area
  padding (matches iOS/Android conventions); above it centers as a
  modal card. Escape key closes via phx-window-keydown so keyboard
  users have parity with backdrop click.
--%>
<div
  :if={@reaction_picker_for}
  id="reaction-picker"
  class="reaction-picker fixed inset-0 z-50"
  phx-window-keydown="close_reaction_picker"
  phx-key="Escape"
>
  <div
    class="reaction-picker-scrim absolute inset-0 bg-base-content/20"
    phx-click="close_reaction_picker"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>
  <%!--
    `role="dialog"` without `aria-modal="true"` is an intentional
    downgrade: we don't yet have a focus trap or return-focus-on-close,
    so claiming modality to assistive tech would be a false promise.
    Full focus management lands in PR B (search + a11y feature pass).
  --%>
  <div
    class="reaction-picker-panel rounded-lg border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-3 shadow-xl"
    role="dialog"
    aria-label="Add reaction"
  >
    <div class="mb-2 flex items-center justify-between">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-base-content/60">
        Add reaction
      </span>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="close_reaction_picker"
        title="Close"
        aria-label="Close reaction picker"
        class="reaction-picker-close rounded p-1 text-base-content/50 hover:bg-base-200 hover:text-base-content"
      >
        <span class="hero-x-mark size-5"></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="reaction-picker-grid">
      <button
        :for={emoji <- @reaction_picker_emojis}
        type="button"
        phx-click="react"
        phx-value-message-id={@reaction_picker_for}
        phx-value-emoji={emoji}
        title={"React with #{emoji}"}
        aria-label={"React with #{emoji}"}
        class="reaction-picker-tile rounded hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors"
      >
        {emoji}
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<%!--
  Quick-react popover (mobile). Triggered by double-tap on a message
  authored by someone else — see the `LongpressMenu` JS hook, which
  despite the legacy name now listens for a double-tap gesture rather
  than a 450ms hold. Scrim + blur fade in, target message clones and
  animates to viewport center via `MessageLift`, and the emoji pill
  floats above the lifted clone. Pill position is driven by
  `--clone-half-h`, set by the hook at mount. The historical action
  card (Copy / Open in thread / Pin) was removed: Copy duplicated the
  browser's native selection menu on mobile, and Pin was frequently
  triggered by accident. Thread-open is deferred to a follow-up UX
  pass; desktop still exposes both via the hover action bar.
--%>
<div
  :if={@longpress_menu_for}
  id="longpress-menu"
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50"
  role="dialog"
  aria-label="Message actions"
  data-target-message-id={@longpress_menu_for}
  phx-hook="MessageLift"
>
  <div
    class="absolute inset-0 longpress-scrim"
    phx-click="close_longpress_menu"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
  </div>

  <%!-- Emoji quick-react pill, floats above the lifted clone.
       Each tap fires `react` (persists the reaction via Chat.toggle_reaction
       → close_picker/1 closes both reaction_picker_for and longpress_menu_for). --%>
  <div class="longpress-pill" role="group" aria-label="Quick reactions">
    <button
      :for={emoji <- ~w(👍 🎉 ✅ ❤️ 😂 🙏)}
      type="button"
      class="longpress-pill-btn"
      title={"React with #{emoji}"}
      phx-click="react"
      phx-value-message-id={@longpress_menu_for}
      phx-value-emoji={emoji}
    >
      {emoji}
    </button>
    <div class="longpress-pill-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="longpress-pill-btn longpress-pill-more"
      title="More emoji"
      aria-label="More emoji"
      phx-click={
        JS.push("open_reaction_picker", value: %{"message-id" => @longpress_menu_for})
        |> JS.push("close_longpress_menu")
      }
    >
      <span class="hero-plus size-4"></span>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>

<.image_lightbox url={@lightbox_url} />

<%!-- Per-message actions sheet (task 019e0f29 Stage 3 — fixes Marlowe's bug
     report that the chat-message 3-dot dropdown didn't open on touch).
     Single Sheet at the page bottom, sourced by :open_message_actions_id;
     same pattern as the per-row task-actions sheet from Task 05 Stage 2.

     Actions are the chat-message hover-toolbar's text-able actions
     (Copy / Pin / Reply). Quick-emoji react row + reaction picker are
     deferred — they'd need their own design beyond a simple action list.
     The Edit item lands in Stage 4 once the editable-messages contract
     ships. --%>
<%!-- Listener for scroll-to-message events from the correction header
     (task 019e0f29 Stage 6, contract Section D.4). Hidden div; the
     ChatScrollToMessage hook drives smooth scroll + brief pulse. --%>
<div id="chat-scroll-to-message-listener" phx-hook="ChatScrollToMessage" class="hidden"></div>

<%!-- Version history popover (task 019e0f29 Stage 6, contract Section D.2).
     Surfaces when @version_history is set (clicking the `(edited)` affix on
     a message bubble). --%>
<PlatformWeb.Components.ChatVersionHistory.chat_version_history
  open={@version_history != nil}
  versions={(@version_history && @version_history.versions) || []}
/>

<%!-- Removal-warning modal (task 019e0f29 Stage 5, contract Section F.4
     Policy 4). Surfaces only when the user's edit shortens / removes
     content. Copy locked in by Marlowe on 2026-05-11 review round 1:
     terse, factual, no editorial. Buttons: Cancel (keeps editor open
     with the user's draft) / Edit anyway (fires the actual edit). --%>
<div
  :if={@pending_save_edit}
  id="edit-removal-warning"
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center bg-black/60 backdrop-blur-sm"
  phx-window-keydown="cancel_save_edit"
  phx-key="escape"
>
  <div
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="edit-removal-warning-title"
    class="w-full max-w-md rounded-2xl border border-base-content/10 bg-base-100 p-5 shadow-xl"
  >
    <h2 id="edit-removal-warning-title" class="text-base font-semibold text-base-content">
      Edit removes text.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70">
      Agents that already read this still have the original in their memory.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="cancel_save_edit"
        class="rounded-md px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/70 hover:bg-base-300 hover:text-base-content transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        Cancel
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        phx-click="confirm_save_edit"
        class="rounded-md bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-primary-content hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
      >
        Edit anyway
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<.sheet
  :if={@open_message_actions_id}
  id="message-actions-sheet"
  open={true}
  placement={:bottom}
  on_close="close_message_actions"
>
  <:title>Message actions</:title>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("toggle_inline_thread",
          value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id}
        )
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-chat-bubble-left-right size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Reply in thread</span>
    </button>
    <button
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("pin_toggle", value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id})
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-bookmark size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Pin / Unpin</span>
    </button>
    <%!-- Edit affordance — Policy 3 of the editable-messages contract
         (own non-agent text messages only). The message struct is lifted
         into @open_message_actions_msg by the open_message_actions
         handler so the visibility filter can be evaluated at template
         render time. The hover-pencil affordance on the chat row was
         removed in task 019e2452; this sheet item is now the SOLE edit
         entry point on all viewports. --%>
    <button
      :if={
        @open_message_actions_msg && @current_participant &&
          @open_message_actions_msg.participant_id == @current_participant.id &&
          @open_message_actions_msg.content_type == "text"
      }
      type="button"
      phx-click={
        Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("edit_message_clicked",
          value: %{"message-id" => @open_message_actions_id}
        )
        |> Phoenix.LiveView.JS.push("close_message_actions")
      }
      class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-left text-base-content hover:bg-base-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary/60"
    >
      <span class="hero-pencil-square size-5 text-base-content/70"></span>
      <span class="font-medium">Edit message</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</.sheet>
